            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0700" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/181: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-15T19:00:00-06:00">June 15, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 16—11:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. I returned to Tegucigalpa today after a very worthwhile trip on the north
                    coast. Arranged with the Captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Richmond</hi>
                    and Consuls about evacuating Americans and other protection measures in event of
                    danger. Conferred with Consular Inspector Davis.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
